> - Spells...? not until I get a good one?

Spells are good.  But I would choose good AC and lots of daggers over
spells any day.  Even for a wizard.


> - Daggers definetly beat crossbow?

Daggers have a nice to-hit bonus and Rogues have the chance of throwing 
one extra dagger.  If you end up throwing most of your daggers, you can 
still keep one (or two with two-weapon) in reserve to melee with, 
without having to use different skill slots for missile and melee.

It looks to me that, if you are guaranteed to hit, crossbow will do more 
damage, even taking the extra dagger into account.  But in the early 
game, I am confident that the dagger's to-hit bonus outweighs this.
Also crossbow bolts will slowly disappear, while daggers are forever.


